@node emacsctl Contexts
@section emacsctl Contexts

@file{~/.config/cmacs/emacsctl.yaml} (override per-invocation with
@option{--config PATH} or globally with @env{EMACSCTL_CONFIG}).
Parsed with yaml-glib; @emph{unknown keys are ignored, never
errors}, so the schema can grow without breaking older clients.

Generate a commented starter file with @code{emacsctl config init}:

@example
apiVersion: cmacs.org/v1
kind: EmacsctlConfig
current-context: local
contexts:
  - name: local
    instance: primary      # primary | auto (newest) | <pid>
    output: table          # table | json | yaml | raw
  # - name: laptop
  #   host: user@@laptop   # tunneled via `emacsctl proxy` over ssh
  #   instance: auto
aliases:
  # b: get buffers
settings:
  timeout: 30
@end example

A context bundles @code{name}, @code{instance}, optional ssh
@code{host}, default @code{output} format, and a per-context
@code{timeout}.

@example
emacsctl config get-contexts        # NAME / CURRENT table
emacsctl config use-context laptop  # persisted; comments survive
emacsctl config view                # print the file
emacsctl --context laptop get buffers
@end example

@code{config use-context} rewrites only the @code{current-context:}
line textually, so comments in the file are preserved.

Top-level @code{aliases:} maps a word to a replacement command line,
expanded in command position only: with @code{b: get buffers},
@code{emacsctl b -o json} runs @code{get buffers -o json}.

Instance auto-selection (@code{instance: auto} or nothing
configured): @env{CMACS_DBUS_NAME} if set; else the single
@code{org.cmacs.Editor.Pid*} instance if exactly one exists; with
several instances running, the @emph{newest} one (most recently
started process, by kernel start time); no instances at all is exit
4.  Use @code{instance: primary} / @option{--instance primary} to
pin the well-known @code{org.cmacs.Editor} holder instead, or an
explicit PID for full control.
